      "body": "## Bug\n\n`OneCycle._initialize_momentum()` sets the optimizer's initial `beta1` to `cycle_min_mom`, but the inverse-cycling schedule starts at `cycle_max_mom` (at `scale_factor=0`, `get_mom()` returns `max_mom - 0 = max_mom`). This means the first `optimizer.step()` consumes a different momentum than the schedule intends, causing a training-correctness divergence from the second update onward.\n\nFixes #8951\n\n## Root cause\n\n```python\n# Before (line 576):\nfor momentum, group in zip(self.min_moms, optimizer.param_groups):\n    group['betas'] = momentum\n\n# After:\nfor momentum, group in zip(self.max_moms, optimizer.param_groups):\n    group['betas'] = momentum\n```\n\nThe LR/momentum symmetry: LR initialises at `min` and ramps up; momentum initialises at `max` and ramps down. `_initialize_lr` correctly sets `min_lrs`; `_initialize_momentum` was incorrectly mirroring that instead of inverting.\n\n## Changes\n\n1. **`deepspeed/runtime/lr_schedules.py`**: Initialise optimizer betas from `self.max_moms` instead of `self.min_moms`\n2. **Docstring**: Remove \"Initial momentum\" wording from `cycle_min_mom` param (it's the lower bound, not the initial value)\n3. **`tests/unit/runtime/test_lr_schedulers.py`**: Fix `test_one_cycle_accepts_per_group_lr_and_momentum_lists` which asserted the wrong initial betas, and add `test_one_cycle_initial_optimizer_momentum_matches_schedule` verifying optimizer state matches the scheduler's reported momentum at construction",
      "changedFiles": 2,
