  "inline_comments": [
    {
      "body": "**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Add a training-loop regression for initial momentum**\n\nWhen `cycle_min_mom != cycle_max_mom`, this fix changes Adam’s first-moment state on the first update and subsequent parameter updates, but this test only checks constructor metadata and never performs an optimizer update. The existing `TestOneCycle.test_mom` asserts scheduler-reported momenta rather than optimizer state or parameter values, so its assertions also pass with the faulty initialization. Root `AGENTS.md` requires integration coverage for training-loop contract changes; extend that training test with deterministic updates and compare optimizer state or parameters against an independent Adam reference initialized with `cycle_max_mom`.\n\nAGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L81-L81](https://github.com/deepspeedai/DeepSpeed/blob/ba1d13223521e5e65bf5743c25179d78c07fc6a3/AGENTS.md#L81-L81)\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\n<!-- codex-code-review-finding:v1 -->",
      "created_at": "2026-11-02T00:23:04Z",
      "diff_hunk": "@@ -858,6 +858,24 @@ def test_one_cycle_accepts_per_group_lr_and_momentum_lists():\n     assert [group[\"betas\"][0] for group in optimizer.param_groups] == pytest.approx([0.9, 0.95])\n \n \n+def test_one_cycle_initial_optimizer_momentum_matches_schedule():\n+    param = torch.nn.Parameter(torch.zeros(1))\n+    optimizer = torch.optim.Adam([param], lr=0.1, betas=(0.9, 0.99))\n+    scheduler = OneCycle(optimizer=optimizer,\n+                         cycle_min_lr=0.1,\n+                         cycle_max_lr=0.2,\n+                         cycle_first_step_size=4,\n+                         cycle_second_step_size=4,\n+                         cycle_min_mom=0.8,\n+                         cycle_max_mom=0.9)\n+\n+    reported = scheduler.get_mom()[0][0]\n+    actual = optimizer.param_groups[0]['betas'][0]\n+    assert actual == pytest.approx(reported), (\n+        f\"optimizer beta1 ({actual}) != scheduler.get_mom() ({reported})\")\n+    assert actual == pytest.approx(0.9)",
